 ### [Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) Representation](12096-neural-radiance-field-nerf-representation.md)
-Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) represent a 3D scene as a continuous volumetric function parameterized by a multi-layer perceptron (MLP), enabling the synthesis of novel views from a sparse set of input images by solving the volume rendering integral. Unlike explicit representations such as [3D Gaussian Splatting](12052-3d-gaussian-splatting-optimization.md) which store millions of discrete blobs, NeRF stores the scene implicitly within a neural network, allowing for high-fidelity, view-dependent appearance modeling with significantly lower memory footprint, albeit at the cost of slower rendering and training times.
+See [Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) Representation](12096-neural-radiance-field-nerf-representation.md).
 
