-#### CP-SLAM
-CP-SLAM is a neural point-based hybrid neural field SLAM system enabling multi-agent cooperative localization and mapping with loop closure [S3]. It uses a keyframe-associated neural point representation inspired by PointNeRF, allowing per-point features to be adjusted during pose graph optimization [S3]. It employs a two-stage distributed-to-centralized training scheme: initial decoders are trained separately for each agent, then fused and fine-tuned jointly [S3]. It integrates odometry, loop detection, sub-map fusion, and global refinement into a unified framework [S3].
+**Comparison**
+On EuRoC Machine Hall (Stereo Depth), ATE RMSE (m): ORB-SLAM3 0.052, Ours 3.190. Point-SLAM fails on all sequences [S2, unofficial]. ORB-SLAM achieves best ATE, but the combined approach shows no significant difference in rendering metrics compared to unified 3DGS SLAM. The unified approach is preferred for exploring 3DGS throughout the entire algorithm [S2, unofficial].
 
-#### MNE-SLAM
-MNE-SLAM is the first fully distributed multi-agent neural SLAM framework enabling accurate collaborative mapping and robust camera tracking without centralized training or raw data exchange [S3]. It uses a triplane+MLP hybrid neural field representation as a mapping module [S3]. It introduces an intra-to-inter loop closure strategy to reduce pose drift and align submaps across agents through peer-to-peer feature sharing and global consistency loss [S3].
+### CP-SLAM
