-#### HERO-SLAM
-HERO-SLAM is a SLAM method employing a novel multiscale patch-based loss that aligns feature points, maps, and RGB-D pixels through warpings [S3]. It uses an INGP-like multiresolution hybrid feature grid+MLP representation for neural SDF learning [S3].
+**Steps**
+*   Uses a keyframe-associated neural point representation inspired by PointNeRF, allowing per-point features to be adjusted during pose graph optimization [S3].
+*   Employs a two-stage distributed-to-centralized training scheme: initial decoders are trained separately for each agent, then fused and fine-tuned jointly [S3].
+*   Integrates odometry, loop detection, sub-map fusion, and global refinement into a unified framework [S3].
 
-#### PIN-SLAM
-PIN-SLAM is a globally consistent SLAM system using a point-based implicit neural (PIN) representation [S3]. It replaces grid structures with neural feature points, offering spatial flexibility and elastic correction during loop closure [S3]. Mapping alternates with odometry [S3]. The mapping step is based on a hybrid neural SDF representation with explicit neural points and implicit MLP decoders [S3]. Odometry is performed correspondence-free via second-order scan-to-map optimization [S3]. A sliding window replay buffer ensures stable incremental updates [S3]. Loop closures trigger pose graph optimization and elastic deformation of neural points, enabling consistent large-scale mapping [S3].
+### MNE-SLAM
